Two answers, read by the shipped blocklist and by the rebuilt allowlist.
Every number below is counted by running both, not typed into this text.

  what the record said              shipped     FINDING  UNSTATED
  uRPF loose, BGP MD5                     2           2         0
  uRPF OFF, BGP UNAUTHENTICATED           0           2         0
  answers the checks never met            0           0         2

The shipped check reported 2 on a device described as middling and 0 on the
same device described as having no source validation and no routing
authentication at all. Making the device worse made the report shorter,
because "none" is not the one string each check recognised.

The rebuilt check reported 2 finding(s) on the first and 2 on the second, and
on answers it had never met it reported 0 finding(s) and 2 unstated --- which
is the difference that matters. An allowlist has nowhere to put an answer it
does not recognise except into the report; a blocklist puts it in the silence,
where it reads as approval.
